  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 653 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D9"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the ketorolac tromethamine shortage on 2018-03-23 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E45", "D19"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Hospira, Inc. plant (FEI 1925262) on the product label was inspected and classified OAI on 2016-06-08, 653 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E31", "E25", "D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The same plant received a Warning Letter on 2017-02-14, 402 days before the posting, and a second OAI inspection ended 2018-08-15, 145 days after the posting.",
      "cites": ["E30", "D10", "E27", "D14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Another Hospira plant (FEI 1021343) on the label had OAI inspections in 2010 and 2011 and a Warning Letter in 2010, all years before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E19", "E9", "E11", "E13", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Nitto Avecia Pharma Services plant (FEI 3012971227) on the label shows only VAI inspections, the latest ending 2020-01-24.",
      "cites": ["E37", "E36"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Baxter Healthcare, Fresenius Kabi, Hikma, Gland Pharma, Sagent, and Hospira all appear on FDA's current shortage list with estimated recoveries ranging from late 2026 to December 2027.",
      "cites": ["E39", "E40", "E41", "E42", "E43", "E44"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to buy from Anthea Pharma Private Limited, which is not on FDA's shortage list today.",
      "cites": ["D20"]
    }
  ]
}
